detailedInstruction:
Now let's write your first Java program! Copy and paste this code into your Hello.java file:

```java
public class Hello {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello World");
    }
}
```

Let me explain each part:
• 'public class Hello' - Creates a class named Hello (must match filename)
• 'public static void main' - The entry point where your program starts
• 'String[] args' - Command line arguments (not used here)
• 'System.out.println' - Prints text to the console
• The curly braces {} group code together

Tip: Java is case-sensitive, so 'System' must have a capital S!
